  <name>puddletag</name>
  <summary>Powerful, simple, audio tag editor</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      puddletag is an audio tag editor for GNU/Linux similar to the Windows
      program Mp3tag. Unlike most taggers for GNU/Linux, it uses a
      spreadsheet-like layout so that all the tags you want to edit by hand
      are visible and easily editable.
    </p>
    <p>
      The usual tag editor features are supported like extracting tag
      information from filenames, renaming files based on their tags by using
      patterns and basic tag editing. Functions can do things like replace
      text, trim it, do case conversions, etc. Actions can automate repetitive
      tasks. Web lookups using AcoustID, Amazon, Discogs, FreeDB and
      MusicBrainz are also supported.
    </p>
  </description>
  <developer id="net.puddletag">
    <name>puddletag developers</name>
  </developer>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">puddletag.desktop</launchable>
  <url type="homepage">https://docs.puddletag.net/</url>
